    "note": [
        {
            "structuredValue": [],
            "parallelValue": [],
            "groupedValue": [],
            "value": "The Sovereignty, Empathy, Education, Determination, and Sisterhood (SEEDS) curriculum is a comprehensive supplementary educational program designed to empower young Indigenous girls, ages 9-13, as they develop fundamental leadership and community service skills. \r\n\r\nRooted in the Medicine Wheel, SEEDS is comprised of four units—Self, Community, Service, and Purpose—that guide participants on a structured journey of self-reflection and growth. Each unit is carefully crafted to fulfill a specific sense, encouraging participants to explore their identities, build strong community ties, engage in meaningful service, and develop a sense of responsibility to the world around them. \r\n\r\nSEEDS is designed to be user-friendly, flexible, and adaptable, allowing facilitators to tailor it to the unique needs and cultural context of their communities. By empowering young Indigenous girls to embrace their heritage, develop leadership skills, and engage meaningfully with their communities, SEEDS seeks to cultivate a new generation of empowered Indigenous leaders who are capable of driving positive change in their communities and beyond.",
            "type": "abstract",
            "identifier": [],
            "note": [],
            "appliesTo": []
        },
